finding={'id':'Q353','title':'Concurrent Commons parking exceeds its record and byte bounds','source':'crates/moot/commons/src/parking.rs:253,267,281,291','status':'reproduced unchanged current private Parking module over exact retained suppliers and real MemoryBackend','evidence':'Two valid signed operations from different authors both read an empty parking slot list before either writes. Each park call returns true and commits its own unchanged atomic batch. With max_records1, final status is parked2 and evicted0. With max_bytes equal to the larger individual encoded operation, both individually fit but the final byte sum exceeds that bound. Sequential arrivals under max_records1 leave parked1 and evicted1. Slot/occupancy reads are outside the write batch, so atomic apply does not make the read/modify/write decision atomic. The scheduling wrapper changes only the order of list completion and delegates actual MemoryBackend storage/write batches.','scope':'Three deterministic private-module cases, CPU and in-memory storage. No whole Commons, live LogSync, joined host, physical carrier, durable disk or observed large-memory pressure. Record encodings legitimately have different lengths; corrected byte fixture uses max(individual lengths) and their actual sum.','verification':NAME,'diagnostics':['commons_parking_probe_v3_receipt.json'],'repair_triage':{'disposition':'documented under active read-only source audit','reason':'Serialize occupancy/slot conflict, eviction counter and insertion through one backend-owned transaction across every writer for the same parking prefix. Backend::transact is the existing read-plus-write owner; preserve typed refusal when unavailable. A lock only on one Parking clone would miss independently constructed owners over the same backend. Cover count, bytes and same-slot concurrent outcomes before broadening acceptance claims.'}}
notes['findings'].append(finding)
for f in notes['findings']:
    if f['id']=='Q352':
        f.setdefault('followup_evidence',[]).append({'verification':NAME,'diagnostic':gap_name,'detail':'Whole Commons source review complete. Public callback key-replacement cases and full-library runner are prepared but not executed: bounded retained-supplier selection could not prove the chosen Gemot/Insigne fingerprint family coherent. No fresh dependency build was substituted.'})
rows=[
('Graph profiles share one causal and remove-wins meaning','Both plaintext and encrypted authoring call the root author_batch and fold_with_authority.',['crates/moot/commons/src/lib.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/encrypted.rs'],'CausalIndex and RemovalIndex are built once per fold and reused across batches. Only concurrent inserts of removed identities are suppressed; observing inserts can recreate. Signer-scoped contiguous edge counters have one shared validation owner. Fingerprint-based tests compare nodes/title/tags and edge class, not every possible facet/identity/property; source tests separately exercise facets and writer-scoped IDs.'),
('Writer attestation verification has shared and chat-local implementations','Graph stable_subject delegates to stickleback::stable_writer_subject; chat stable_chat_author repeats the binding checks.',['crates/moot/commons/src/lib.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/chat.rs'],'The graph profiles reuse a common helper for signer, attestation and domain salt; chat reconstructs those checks directly with separate errors and constructor behavior. This is a genuine duplicate binding recipe to track, not proof of a cryptographic bypass. The graph derived_writer constructor checks the derived key but does not separately compare the attestation root to IdentityProvider::master_public_key, while chat for_identity does.'),
('Authority adapters intentionally expose different conflict precedence','GemotAuthorityView checks coverage first; ServitorAuthorityView checks the supplied revoked-subject set first.',['crates/moot/commons/src/lib.rs'],'Both implement CommonsAuthority over retained facts, with explicit subject/capability/mode. A current valid alternative grant wins in the Gemot adapter; the coarse Servitor subject revocation dominates provider coverage. They are alternative host interpretations, not one automatically equivalent authority view. Caller choice and semantic scope must remain explicit rather than inferring identical results from the shared trait.'),
('Compatibility materialization is not communal membership authority','materialize/projection default to structural AllowAllAuthority; governed callers opt into projection_with_authority.',['crates/moot/commons/src/lib.rs'],'Public API comments correctly require communal products to use the authority-classified route. Retention is separate from revocation visibility and causal readiness. The thin CommonsPolicy prose still calls this a probe although the package now positions itself as reusable product infrastructure. No current product misrouting is asserted without its consumer trace.'),
('Parking occupancy decisions are separate from atomic writes','Parking reads slots and eviction totals before Backend::apply.',['crates/moot/commons/src/parking.rs'],'Q353 reproduces record and byte bound violations under two permitted overlapping writers. Real MemoryBackend batches remain atomic; the missing transaction is the read/modify/write decision. Readmission notices duplicate slots as a lost race, but that later cleanup does not establish insertion-time bounds or a globally serialized slot owner.'),
('Readmission reuses ordinary admission and carries deletion in the insert batch','Parking::readmit hands an unparking WriteOp to OperationProcessor::process_with_writes.',['crates/moot/commons/src/parking.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/encrypted.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/chat.rs'],'This is actual shared storage publication for inserted records. Already-stored/refused records use later standalone deletion, and unreadable/invalid parked encodings are dropped and counted as refused. Q353 diagnostics exercise park/status only, not readmission or crash behavior; source comments about one-commit insertion need their separately scoped processor evidence.'),
('Epoch release relies on a complete caller-supplied lane report set','release_epochs preserves current and every supplied needed/unreported epoch.',['crates/moot/commons/src/pruning.rs'],'A report that omits an epoch keeps it with an Unreported reason. The function does not discover missing lanes, validate a common key-snapshot generation or require a nonempty report list; the host owns that completeness and lifecycle. Empty reports vacuously release noncurrent epochs. No real host omitted-lane loss is asserted here.'),
('Pruning test helper serialization is not durable session persistence','The test-only host::apply round-trips GroupSession bytes and refreshes GroupKeys.',['crates/moot/commons/src/pruning.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/chat.rs'],'The helper says persist but performs to_bytes/from_bytes in memory. A chat test uses a Redb-backed operation store while separately round-tripping group session bytes; this does not prove durable key/session publication or power-cut recovery. Production pruning docs show a caller save step, rather than supplying that durable owner here.'),
('Sans-I/O control scope is narrower than the package dependency cone','call.rs owns pure control folding, inside a Commons package requiring graph, stores, Gemot and network suppliers.',['crates/moot/commons/Cargo.toml','crates/moot/commons/src/call.rs','crates/moot/commons/src/lib.rs'],'Pure control grammar describes module runtime behavior, not an independently buildable leaf crate. Generic CommonsAuthority already exists alongside the direct Gemot adapter dependency. The pending Q352 full-owner diagnostic could not select one coherent retained Gemot/Insigne family; this is a build-evidence limitation, not a demonstrated current Cargo defect or a reason to copy the control/authority logic elsewhere.'),
]
entries=[{'id':f'A{991+i}','domain':d,'claim':c,'implementations':paths,'assessment':a,'state':'Commons source complete; three fresh unchanged Parking module audit cases; full-owner authoring probe unexecuted','verification':NAME} for i,(d,c,paths,a) in enumerate(rows)];authority['entries'].extend(entries)
completed={'prefix':area,'files':9,'chars':341386,'verification':NAME,'basis_commit':head,'qualification':'Every inventoried Commons source file fully reviewed at current matching hashes. Only Parking park/status executed in this pass, over retained suppliers; the original whole-library suites were not run.'}
